7.020</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17854845</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilbert</surname><given-names>S. J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shallice</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2002</year>). <article-title>Task switching: a PDP model</article-title>. <source>Cogn. Psychol.</source><volume>44</volume>, <fpage>297</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>337</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/cogp.2001.0770</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luks</surname><given-names>T. L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Simpson</surname><given-names>G. V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Feiwell</surname><given-names>R. J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>W. L.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2002</year>). <article-title>Evidence for anterior cingulate cortex involvement in monitoring preparatory attentional set</article-title>. <source>Neuroimage</source><volume>17</volume>, <fpage>792</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>802</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1053-8119(02)91210-3</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12377154</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mayr</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name><name><surname>Diedrichsen</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ivry</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Keele</surname><given-names>S. W.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2006</year>). <article-title>Dissociating task-set selection from task-set inhibition in the prefrontal cortex</article-title>. <source>J. Cogn. Neurosci.</source><volume>18</volume>, <fpage>14</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1162/089892906775250085</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16417679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mecklinger</surname><given-names>A. D.</given-names></name><name><surname>von Cramon</surname><given-names>D. Y.</given-names></name><name><surname>Springer</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Matthes-von Cramon</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1999</year>). <article-title>Executive control functions in task switching: evidence from brain injured patients</article-title>. <source>J. Clin. Exp. Neuropsychol.</source><volume>21</volume>, <fpage>606</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>619</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10572281</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meiran</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1996</year>). <article-title>Reconfiguration of processing mode prior to task performance</article-title>. <source>J. Exp. Psychol. Learn. Mem. Cogn.</source><volume>22</volume>, <fpage>1432</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1442</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0278-7393.22.6.1423</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meiran</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chorev</surname><given-names>Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sapir</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2000</year>). <article-title>Component processes in task switching</article-title>. <source>Cogn. Psychol.</source><volume>41</volume>, <fpage>211</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/cogp.2000.0736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Milner</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1963</ye